    "vertices": "V = (P - Z) * S + Z + C"
  },
  "max_faces": 715827881,
  "proof": "For each valid band, a positive-positive band has 2S faces and a pole-adjacent band has S; there are Z pole-adjacent bands. Adding C cap fans gives F. V has one S-vertex ring per nonpole endpoint/profile point, one vertex per pole, and one center per enabled cap. Direct subtraction gives F + 1 - V = S * (P - 2 + C) + 1 - Z - C. For Z=0 this is S*(P-2)+C*(S-1)+1; for Z=1 it is S*(P-2)+C*(S-1); for Z=2, C=0 and P>=3, so it is S*(P-2)-1. Each is nonnegative for the stated domain, so V <= F+1.",
